    "done_when": "scripts/figures_jt60sa_geometry.py loads load_packaged_machine_map('jt-60sa'), opens each phase map (OP1, OP2) through NetCDFTransformEngine.open with the catalogue's description_store_root_path(), dd_version, map and description_store_layout, reads wall, pf_active and magnetics with imas.DBEntry from the opened store's path, passes them to imas_ink.extract.extract_geometry and renders with imas_ink.figures.geometry_figure_mpl in DEFAULT_STYLE, holding no colour, label or style constant of its own and drawing no element itself; it writes exactly two SVG files and no PNG under docs/figures/jt60sa-geometry/: one figure with OP1 and OP2 side by side on two axes sharing one viewport through geometry_figure_mpl's ax argument, and one panel overlaying the two phases with OP2 in DEFAULT_STYLE and OP1 in replace(DEFAULT_STYLE, wall_linestyle=DEFAULT_STYLE.ref_lcfs_linestyle); the script prints per phase the PF coils drawn, the filaments they enclose, the first-wall and vessel-shell contour points, flux loops and probes passed to imas-ink, and these equal the store's counts; docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-geometry-and-signal-figures/jtfig-geometry-figures.html embeds both SVGs with project-absolute src and captions stating which panel is which phase, which contours are the first wall and which the vessel skins, that each coil rectangle outlines one of the 12 PF coils around its 268 filaments in all, that the cryostat-scale passive loop and the sensors EDDB acquires without a facility position are not drawn, and the printed counts; 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests scripts/figures_jt60sa_geometry.py' exits 0",
    "estimated_hours": 1.0,
    "goal": "Render the JT-60SA OP1 and OP2 geometry figures through imas-ink",
